---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const content = `# Authorization Reference

## Authentication vs. authorization

- Authentication verifies the identity of a user or service.
- Authorization determines what that identity can access.

## Three participants

- Client: requests a token and uses it to access a protected resource.
- Resource server: hosts the resource and validates the client token.
- Authorization server: issues tokens to clients.

## Practical rules

- Keep tokens lifetime-limited.
- Grant clients only the scopes they require.
- Treat write access as distinct from read access.
- Revisit service boundaries when one client accumulates too many dependencies.
`;
